.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
# Same class of mistake as the old blanket db/ and fixtures/ rules below: these two are the
# public CockroachDB Cloud root CA cert (ISRG Root X1 -- Let's Encrypt's own root, checked
# 2026-08-12: no private key, nothing sensitive) that workers/, dashboard/, and now agent/'s
# Dockerfile all need present at a known path. A CA cert is public by definition -- verified
# before un-ignoring, not assumed safe. Transient certs fetched fresh per CI run (e.g.
# cluster-ca.crt/target-ca.crt in .github/workflows/*) stay correctly ignored by the blanket
# rule above; only these two checked-in, reused assets are exempted.
!workers/common/certs/*.crt
!dashboard/certs/*.crt
credentials.json

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

node_modules/
.next/
out/
.vercel/

# CDK (infra/) — synth output and the hand-assembled Lambda build dir (infra/build.py)
cdk.out/
infra/.build/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
scratch/

# Demo-video production notes (execution plan / recording run-sheet / narration script) —
# internal working docs for recording the submission video, not project code or evidence;
# don't belong in a public hackathon repo. Listed by exact path, not a blanket *.md rule,
# per this project's own standing rule against blanket gitignores hiding real content.
docs/demo-video-plan.md
docs/demo-video-script.md
docs/demo-video-final-script.md

# db/ holds SQL source (migrations, console-paste chunks) that IS committed —
# only ignore actual local scratch state under it, never the .sql sources.
db/*.db
db/*.sqlite

# fixtures/ holds real captured API responses that ARE committed and cited
# as evidence (e.g. fixtures/cloudapi-backups-basic.json, referenced by
# agent/tools/cloud_api.py and tests/test_cloud_api.py) — same class of
# mistake as the old blanket db/ rule above; checked for secrets before
# un-ignoring (2026-08-11): none found, both files are cluster metadata /
# API response bodies already visible elsewhere in the docs.
